Here, we have the product of two functions $u(x) = 2x$ and $v(x)=	anh x.$ So, we apply the product rule:

$$
 egin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =(2x)^{′}\cdot \operatorname{tanh}⁡x+2x\cdot (\operatorname{tanh}⁡x)^{′} \  & =2\cdot \operatorname{tanh}⁡x+2x\cdot {	ext{\sech}}^{2}x \  & =2\operatorname{tanh}⁡x+2x{	ext{\sech}}^{2}x \  & =2(\operatorname{tanh}⁡x+x{	ext{\sech}}^{2}x)\end{aligned}
$$
